# "cond" a_ssert< "message" reports a failed condition, as written, on
# standard error and goes on; its value is @ (unlike Rust's assert!, it
# never stops the program).
== SOURCE
x := 6
"x > 10" a_ssert< "x is big"
"x > 1" a_ssert< @
x
== EXPAND
x := 6
{ @ -> (x > 10) ? @; []E_RR "assertion failed: x > 10 (x is big) [-e:2]"; @ } @
{ @ -> (x > 1) ? @; []E_RR "assertion failed: x > 1 [-e:3]"; @ } @
x
== RESULT
@
@
6
